<task id="205c" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A39 (H4b per_env_settings — 8 §10.2 live-contract entries + fail-fast + FIC-flap tolerance)</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Per project CLAUDE.md rigor table + root §8.5 TEST-MODIFYING/auth override: A39 tag `auth` (credential-selection settings — `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast is boot-abort-on-misconfig) → code-review + adr-check UNCONDITIONAL. Also modifies handler tests under `tests/**` for FR-C4 verification + FIC-propagation-flap tolerance case → TEST-MODIFYING override row (root §8.5 binding ≥6 months from 2026-06-26). Blast radius: every future customer boot depends on these 8 entries being sourced correctly + in the right order relative to A42's FIC creation.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Sonnet-5 default per project CLAUDE.md §Model tier — A39 is mechanical apply of the well-specified §10.2 live-contract 8-entry delta into an existing handler + manifest (`H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` + `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs`), NOT credential-logic design (that is A38 + A42 on Fable/Opus per remediation plan §8 cost posture). Ordering-guard sequencing + FIC-flap tolerance choice are per-row-specified in the punch entry, not open design. xhigh effort justified by (a) complexity of the FIC-flap tolerance interaction (SF-17 × SF-6 verifier-added case), (b) 8 distinct entries each with a specific `FromHandlerOutput` / literal-string / `FromBicepOutput` sourcing rule, (c) load-bearing-key `required=true` sweep (SF-18 silent-skip trap must not re-emerge).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>ORDERING GUARD (BINDING per auth-v4 §10.2 + remediation plan §7 dependency register): A39 depends on **A38 (task 205a — H4 secret-slot omit)** AND **A42 (task 205b — FIC creation with tenancy guard)** landing FIRST. Setting `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` before the FIC exists boot-loops a fresh stamp (exit-134 class; §5 item 4 verifier-added interaction case). Dispatching A39 in a parallel lane ahead of A42 defeats the entire ordering-guard — do NOT.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A36 (landed 1bc049e4c, BFF UAMI SB Data roles), A37 (landed 1bc049e4c, BFF UAMI Search roles), A38 (task 205a, H4 secret-slot omit), A42 (task 205b, FIC creation + Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy port)</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, code, control-plane, h4b, per-env-settings, credential-selection, fail-fast, fic-flap-tolerance</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4h (per punch row A39 in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply auth-v4 punch row A39 — extend `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` per_env_settings manifest (via `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs`) with the 8 §10.2 live-contract entries: (1) `Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` (ONLY entry in order list — no other providers), (2) `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` (FAIL-FAST — startup abort if any `Credentials__Order__*` entry is not `ManagedIdentityFederated`), (3) `ManagedIdentity__ClientId` = `FromHandlerOutput` (sourced from H2a `uami.bicep` via `InterStepState.MiClientId` — verified field name from `Models/InterStepState.cs:53`), (4) `ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace = <ns>.servicebus.windows.net` (FQNS literal, NOT connection string, NOT KV ref), (5) `Membership__EventPublisher__ServiceBusNamespace = <ns>.servicebus.windows.net`, (6) `Membership__JunctionUpdater__ServiceBusNamespace = <ns>.servicebus.windows.net`, (7) `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled = true`, (8) `AiSafety__ContentSafety__ManagedIdentity__Enabled = true`. Row-execute per 203c pattern: (a) grep-verify current state BEFORE applying (0 of 8 verified per 2026-08-25 grep); (b) confirm dependencies A38 + A42 landed (STOP if not); (c) apply the 8 entries with correct sourcing; (d) each entry MUST be `required=true` (no `required=false` — H4b `:286` silent-skip trap per Section 5 SF-18); (e) implement FIC-propagation-flap tolerance choice (either verified-exchange gate BEFORE settings-apply, OR H4b boot-retry allowance — DOCUMENT which choice + WHY in code comment + task notes); (f) add unit tests exercising the fail-fast path (missing/wrong `Credentials__Order__*` entry → startup abort); (g) add integration test: fresh Model 2 stamp boots with all 8 settings applied post-FIC-verified to `/healthz` 200 within expected window. Publish-size verification: A39 touches BFF-consumed shared code seam (`H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler` runs in L2 but writes into BFF App Service settings) → NFR-01 publish-size ≤60 MB verification REQUIRED per root CLAUDE.md §10 (baseline: 44.96 MB incl. PDBs per 2026-08-13 net10). Amend punch list annotations. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 control-plane handler author + auth-v4 §10.2 live-contract specialist + credential-selection ordering-guard enforcer. Expert in: `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler` + `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest` contract (per_env_settings + secrets manifest split, `required=true` sweep per §5 SF-18); §10.2 live `spaarke-bff-dev` settings contract (verified live 2026-08-24 post-E-3 closure); `InterStepState` field-name plumbing (`MiClientId` = UAMI clientId at `:53` — the FromHandlerOutput source for entry 3); the ordering-guard doctrine ("provision the identity first, then the setting — never the reverse"); the FIC-propagation-flap interaction case (SF-17 × SF-6 verifier-added: ~8 failures over ~130s AADSTS70025 × `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast — a stamp booting inside the window can fail to START); NFR-01 publish-size baseline (44.96 MB incl. PDBs, 2026-08-13 net10 framework-dependent linux-x64); §6.5 conflict resolution record (APPROVED 2026-08-25) — the constraint file rewrite that makes A39 lawful (secret-free is the default; H4 omits — no sentinel; H4b provides the runtime settings that make MI-FIC the ONLY path).</role>

  <goal>H4b `per_env_settings` manifest contains all 8 §10.2 live-contract entries with correct sourcing (`FromHandlerOutput` for `ManagedIdentity__ClientId` — field `InterStepState.MiClientId` per verified read; `FromBicepOutput` or literal for the FQNS entries; literal `true`/`ManagedIdentityFederated` for the flag + order entries). `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast path exercised in unit tests (missing OR wrong `Credentials__Order__*` entry → startup abort observable). Ordering guard enforced: A39 dispatch blocked until A42 confirmed landed (guard implemented via task-execute Step 0 dependency check OR handler test asserting FIC exists BEFORE settings-apply). FIC-propagation-flap window (~130s post-create; AADSTS70025) tolerated: either verified-exchange gate before settings-apply, OR H4b boot-retry allowance — design choice DOCUMENTED in code comment + task notes with rationale (which SF-17×SF-6 mitigation was chosen and why). No load-bearing key marked `required=false` (H4b `:286` silent-skip trap avoided; grep-verified post-edit). `ManagedIdentity__ClientId` sourced `FromHandlerOutput` correctly (H2a `uami.bicep` output → `InterStepState.MiClientId`); test verifies the plumbing does NOT swap in `MiObjectId` (the SF-2 identifier-swap trap). Integration test: fresh Model 2 stamp boots with all 8 settings applied post-FIC-verified, `/healthz` returns 200 within expected window (verify: NOT anonymous-healthz-only — must exercise a credential-level signal per SF-20 / Q11). `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` succeeds after A39 edits; `dotnet test` on the H4b handler test suite passes including new fail-fast + FIC-flap-tolerance cases. Publish-size re-baseline: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/` compressed output reported with delta vs 44.96 MB baseline — MUST stay ≤60 MB ceiling per NFR-01 (expected delta ≈0 MB since A39 only adds handler-side manifest entries; no NuGet adds).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Auth-v4 §10 addendum Δ3 identified 0 of 8 §10.2 live-contract credential-selection settings present in any customer-facing surface (verified 2026-08-25 grep: only older `Graph__ManagedIdentity__*` appear, as comments/test-fixture keys). A fresh customer BFF stamp therefore boots on the secret path even after A36/A37/A38/A42 land — the H3-created FIC is dead weight without these 8 entries wired at runtime. A39 closes Δ3 by extending H4b's `per_env_settings` manifest. ORDERING GUARD (BINDING per §10.2): identity + FIC + RBAC MUST be provisioned BEFORE these settings — "provision the identity first, then the setting — never the reverse". Setting `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` before the FIC exists on a fresh stamp boot-loops it (exit-134 class; verifier-added case §5 item 4). Hence A39 depends on A42 (FIC creation) — this is the verifier-corrected critical-path edge (`A35 → {A38 ∥ A42} → A39 = 11h serial`). Verified handler paths (Glob 2026-08-25): `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BulkAppSettings/H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` + `.../FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs` exist. `InterStepState.MiClientId` field verified at `Models/InterStepState.cs:53` (source for entry 3 — do NOT confuse with `:48 MiObjectId` which is principalId for RBAC assignments per SF-2 identifier-swap trap). Interaction case added post-verifier: FIC propagation flap post-create (~8 failures over ~130s AADSTS70025 — auth-v4 §11 invariant 2 measured value, NOT documented 70021) × `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast means a stamp booting inside the window can fail to START; H4b sequencing must tolerate the window (verified-exchange BEFORE settings-apply OR boot-retry allowance — one is required, both is acceptable, neither is a hard error per §5 item 4 verifier finding). §6.5 conflict resolution (APPROVED owner 2026-08-25) makes A39 lawful: prong 1 of the rewritten never-delete rule states the secret-free contract H4b enforces (`Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` sole entry + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`) — A39 IS the runtime application of that constraint.</background>
