    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="A36" status="landed-1bc049e4c">BFF runtime UAMI granted `Azure Service Bus Data Sender` + `Data Receiver` on the BFF SB namespace (both models). Required BEFORE A39 wires the SB FQNS settings — otherwise BFF boots with FQNS pointing at an unauthorized namespace.</dependency>
      <dependency task="A37" status="landed-1bc049e4c">BFF runtime UAMI granted `Search Index Data Contributor` + `Search Service Contributor` on AI Search (both models). Required BEFORE A39 wires `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` — otherwise BFF boots with MI-search enabled but no role assignments (401 on first index query).</dependency>
      <dependency task="A38" status="required-if-not-landed">Task 205a — H4 secret-slot omit (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` / `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` / `AiSearch--AdminKey`). Required BEFORE A39: if H4 still upserts secret slots AND A39's `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` is applied, the ordered selector cannot distinguish sentinel-vs-real and fails opaquely with `AADSTS7000215` (§9.1 sentinel pathology). If A38 has NOT landed at A39 dispatch time, STOP — this is escalation trigger #1 below.</dependency>
      <dependency task="A42" status="required-if-not-landed">Task 205b — FIC creation with `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` port + AADSTS70025 exact-match retry + exit 0/1/2 discipline. Required BEFORE A39: if no working FIC exists AND A39's `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` is applied, a fresh stamp boot-loops (exit-134 class). This is the verifier-corrected critical-path edge — do NOT dispatch A39 in a parallel lane ahead of A42. If A42 has NOT landed at A39 dispatch time, STOP — escalation trigger #2 below.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §10.2 ORDERING GUARD (BINDING per punch row A39 + remediation plan §7)">Identity + FIC + RBAC MUST be provisioned BEFORE these settings. "Provision the identity first, then the setting — never the reverse." Concretely: A36 + A37 + A38 + A42 MUST all be landed before A39 dispatches. Setting `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` before the FIC exists boot-loops a fresh stamp (exit-134 class). This is a HARD gate — Step 0 verifies + STOPS if not met.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §5 SF-18 (H4b `:286` silent-skip trap; punch row A39 + remediation plan §5)">No load-bearing key may be `required=false`. H4b line 286 silently skips missing optional entries — a mis-flagged optional per-env key converts hard failure into silent omission. All 8 §10.2 entries MUST be `required=true`. Grep-verify post-edit: zero `required=false` (or equivalent) on the 8 new entries.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §10.2 live-contract (verified against `spaarke-bff-dev` 2026-08-24)">Entry 1 `Graph__Credentials__Order__0` MUST equal literal `ManagedIdentityFederated` — MUST be the ONLY `Credentials__Order__*` entry (no `__1`, `__2`, etc. — the ordered selector fails opaquely if any non-MI-FIC provider is listed under `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`). Entry 2 `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity` MUST equal literal `true` (fail-fast — startup abort if entry 1 constraint violated). Entries 4/5/6 FQNS MUST be `<ns>.servicebus.windows.net` format — NOT a connection string, NOT a KV reference. Entries 7/8 MUST be literal `true`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="verified `Models/InterStepState.cs:53` 2026-08-25">Entry 3 `ManagedIdentity__ClientId` MUST source `FromHandlerOutput` field name **`InterStepState.MiClientId`** (UAMI clientId — property at line 53). Do NOT use `MiObjectId` (line 48 — that is principalId for RBAC assignments; substituting it triggers the SF-2 identifier-swap trap: everything creates successfully and fails only at token exchange with `AADSTS700213` wrong-subject). Include a test verifying the plumbing does not swap the two.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§6.5 resolution record APPROVED 2026-08-25 (`notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md`)">The rewritten constraint file's prong 1 mandates the exact contract A39 delivers: `Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` as the ONLY entry + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`. A39 IS the runtime application of that prong. H4 (A38) omits the secret slot — no sentinel — per prong 1 also. Do NOT re-introduce older `Graph__ManagedIdentity__*` keys (grep-verified 2026-08-25: appear only as comments/test-fixture keys; the new contract is `Graph__Credentials__Order__0` + `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity` — NOT the older shape).</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §11 invariant 2 measured (punch row A42 + remediation plan §5 item 4 verifier addition)">FIC propagation flaps post-create (~8 failures over ~130s AADSTS70025 — measured; NOT the documented AADSTS70021). Interaction with `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast: a stamp booting inside the flap window can fail to START. H4b sequencing MUST tolerate the window: EITHER (a) verified-exchange gate BEFORE settings-apply (H4b waits for A42's post-App-Service verification recorded output before writing the 8 entries), OR (b) H4b boot-retry allowance (BFF startup retries FIC exchange on AADSTS70025 for the propagation window before fail-fast fires). Choice MUST be documented in code comment + task notes with rationale — do NOT silently ship neither.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF Hygiene NFR-01">A39 touches BFF-consumed shared runtime settings (handler runs in L2 but writes into BFF App Service settings; a broken A39 boot-aborts BFF). MUST run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/` + measure compressed output + report absolute size + delta vs 44.96 MB baseline in task summary. Threshold: ≥+5 MB single-task delta → explicit justification; ≥55 MB cumulative → architecture review; ≥60 MB → HARD STOP. Expected delta ≈0 MB (handler-side manifest entries only; no NuGet adds).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 auth-tagged unconditional code-review + adr-check (project CLAUDE.md §8.5 override)">A39 tag `auth` (credential-selection + fail-fast). Rigor FULL. code-review + adr-check MUST run at Step 9.5 — NOT skippable. Also TEST-MODIFYING override row (root §8.5) applies since A39 adds unit + integration tests: unconditional.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification">A39 EXTENDS existing `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler` (task 201, landed) + `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest` (existing) — NO new component surface. Answer §11 three-question template in `<notes>` section: Existing (H4b handler + manifest exist), Extension (adds 8 §10.2 entries to existing manifest — not a new manifest kind), Cost-of-doing-nothing (fresh customer BFF boots on secret path; §10.5 silent-fail traps re-emerge; deferred loud failure at cutover per SF-17).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§5 SF-20 (Deploy-AllIndexes silent-fallback) + Q11 (BFF warmup credential self-proof)">Integration test for A39 MUST NOT assert only anonymous `/healthz` 200 — that endpoint exercises no credential and error-open endpoints turn downstream failures into 200s (auth-v4 031 §5.3/§5.5). The integration test MUST exercise a credential-level signal (e.g. a Graph OBO call, a Dataverse app-only read, or a SB send) to confirm the 8 settings are not just present but WORKING. Q11 (BFF warmup self-proof ownership) is queued for Phase-F but the acceptance-level version applies here: no green-on-status-code-alone.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">A39 does NOT touch `.claude/**` — safe for sub-agent dispatch. Punch list annotation writes to `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` (project-scoped notes, not `.claude/`).</constraint>
  </constraints>

