  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load + ordering-guard gate">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, xhigh effort; auth-tagged → code-review + adr-check unconditional per project CLAUDE.md §8.5). Load knowledge files (punch rows draft, remediation plan §5/§7/§8, §6.5 resolution record, open-questions Q9/Q11). **HARD GATE**: verify A38 (task 205a) landed AND A42 (task 205b) landed via git log OR TASK-INDEX.md check. If EITHER is not landed, STOP + emit escalation trigger #1 or #2 (do NOT proceed — setting `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` before FIC + before H4 omit boot-loops fresh stamps per §5 item 4). Also verify A36 + A37 landed at `1bc049e4c` (per punch row header).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current state BEFORE applying (row A39 executor obligation)">Run row-specific greps to confirm the 0-of-8 starting state: (a) `Grep -r "Graph__Credentials__Order__0" src/` — expect zero customer-facing surface matches (older `Graph__ManagedIdentity__*` may appear as comments/test-fixture keys; that is the expected pre-A39 state); (b) `Grep -r "RequireSecretFreeIdentity" src/` — expect zero; (c) `Grep -r "ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace" src/` — expect zero customer-facing surface matches; (d) `Grep -r "AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled" src/` — expect zero; (e) `Grep -r "AiSafety__ContentSafety__ManagedIdentity__Enabled" src/` — expect zero. If any UNEXPECTED matches (e.g. a partial from a parallel session), STOP + reconcile against source-of-truth before proceeding. Read `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` + `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs` end-to-end; identify the exact insertion pattern for a new entry (the existing manifest DSL for `required=true`/`FromHandlerOutput`/`FromBicepOutput`/literal). Read `InterStepState.cs:48-55` and re-confirm `MiClientId` (line 53) is the FromHandlerOutput field for entry 3 (NOT `MiObjectId` line 48 — SF-2 identifier-swap trap).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Design the FIC-flap tolerance choice (SF-17 × SF-6 interaction case)">Choose EITHER (a) verified-exchange gate BEFORE settings-apply — H4b waits for A42's post-App-Service exchange verification recorded output (persisted in Cosmos ProvisioningRun state) before writing the 8 entries; safe against propagation flap by construction, adds ~130s to critical path, OR (b) H4b boot-retry allowance — BFF startup retries FIC exchange on AADSTS70025 (exact-match — NOT substring, per SF-6) for the propagation window (~130s / ~8 attempts) before `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast fires; keeps H4b provisioning fast but adds BFF-side retry logic. Document choice + rationale in a header comment in `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` (or the manifest file) referencing "§5 item 4 verifier addition". Rationale MUST address: (i) which failure mode is worse (deferred settings-apply vs BFF retry logic in critical path); (ii) how the choice interacts with Q11 (BFF warmup credential self-proof — Phase-F obligation); (iii) whether the choice needs re-visiting in Phase-F.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Checkpoint (after Step 0-2 — dependency-gate + design)">Run `context-handoff` (silent — brief "checkpoint" ack).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Apply entries 1 + 2 (credential-order + fail-fast)">EDIT `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs` (or the handler's inline manifest — whichever holds the per_env_settings entries): add (1) `Graph__Credentials__Order__0` = literal `ManagedIdentityFederated`, `required=true`; (2) `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity` = literal `true`, `required=true`. Ensure NO other `Credentials__Order__*` entries exist (grep post-edit); if the older `Graph__ManagedIdentity__*` keys are present in the manifest, DO NOT touch them here — they are separately handled by A38 comment sweep (per §6.5 resolution EDIT companion sweep table, only rewrite `never_delete` annotations; older key removal is out of scope for A39).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Apply entry 3 (ManagedIdentity__ClientId FromHandlerOutput MiClientId)">EDIT to add (3) `ManagedIdentity__ClientId` = `FromHandlerOutput` sourced from `InterStepState.MiClientId` (field name verified at `Models/InterStepState.cs:53`), `required=true`. Use the exact same DSL pattern the manifest already uses for other `FromHandlerOutput` entries. Add an inline comment: `// SF-2 identifier-swap trap: MUST be MiClientId (clientId), NOT MiObjectId (principalId at line 48). Wrong field → AADSTS700213 wrong-subject at exchange.`</step>
    <step order="6" name="Apply entries 4/5/6 (ServiceBus FQNS × 3)">EDIT to add (4) `ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace`, (5) `Membership__EventPublisher__ServiceBusNamespace`, (6) `Membership__JunctionUpdater__ServiceBusNamespace` — all three sourced as `<ns>.servicebus.windows.net` FQNS format (NOT connection string, NOT KV ref). Sourcing: prefer `FromHandlerOutput` off H2a's SB namespace name output (concatenated with `.servicebus.windows.net` suffix) OR `FromBicepOutput` — whichever matches the existing manifest DSL pattern. All three `required=true`.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Apply entries 7 + 8 (MI enablement flags for AiSearch + AiSafety)">EDIT to add (7) `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled` = literal `true`, `required=true`; (8) `AiSafety__ContentSafety__ManagedIdentity__Enabled` = literal `true`, `required=true`. Post-edit grep-verify: `Grep "required=false" H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs` → confirm ZERO matches on the 8 new entries (SF-18 silent-skip trap avoided). Also `Grep "required=true"` and count — expect 8 new occurrences added.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Checkpoint (after 3 apply steps — entries 1-8 landed)">Run `context-handoff`. Report: 8 entries applied; FIC-flap tolerance choice documented; identifier-swap comment in place.</step>
