  <notes>**§11 Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template)**: **Existing** — `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` + `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs` already exist (task 201, landed); the per_env_settings manifest DSL supports `required=true` / `FromHandlerOutput` / `FromBicepOutput` / literal entries; `InterStepState.MiClientId` at line 53 already carries the UAMI clientId output from H2a. **Extension** — A39 adds 8 §10.2 live-contract entries to the existing manifest (mechanical extension of an existing surface, not a new handler or new manifest kind). The one novel piece is the FIC-flap tolerance mechanism (verified-exchange gate OR boot-retry allowance) — this is a per-row-specified interaction case (SF-17 × SF-6 verifier addition to §5 item 4), not a new architectural abstraction. **Cost-of-doing-nothing** — concrete failure modes (per remediation plan §5 item 4 + §8 cost posture): (i) a fresh customer BFF boots on the secret path (H3-created FIC is dead weight; the 8 settings live nowhere customer-facing per 2026-08-25 grep of 0-of-8); (ii) a mis-built FIC incubates until cutover — deferred loud failure at the worst time; (iii) without `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast, a silent regression to secret-path is undetected until first OBO attempt weeks later; (iv) A36/A37/A38/A42 land value = zero without A39 wiring the runtime settings; (v) all 4 credential-selection failure modes named in remediation plan §8 (boot-abort / boots-but-dead / silently-wrong / reviewers-enforce-deleted-object) fire for every future customer. This is BLOCKS-186 (task 186 E2E live-fire); no path to Phase-F sign-off without A39. NOT scope creep — extension of well-scoped existing surface per the three-question test.

**Dependency footnote**: A36 + A37 landed 2026-08-25 at commit `1bc049e4c` (per punch row header). A38 (task 205a) + A42 (task 205b) are the two other 205-series sub-tasks — Step 0 dependency-gate MUST confirm both landed before A39 applies any edits. This is the verifier-corrected critical-path edge — `A35 → {A38 ∥ A42} → A39 = 11h serial` per remediation plan §7 dependency register.

**§6.5 resolution reference**: A39 IS the runtime application of the rewritten constraint's prong 1 (`Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` sole entry + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`). The §6.5 resolution (`notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md`) was APPROVED by owner 2026-08-25 — A39 does not need separate owner sign-off; the resolution's approval covers it.

