**COMPLETION SUMMARY (2026-08-26, SESSION 11)**: 7 of 8 §10.2 entries added to `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` per_env_settings (entry 3, `ManagedIdentity__ClientId`, already existed from task 201 — annotated with SF-2 note only). `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify` exit 0. FIC-flap tolerance = option (b), relying on `HttpHealthzProbe`'s EXISTING 480s backoff budget (no new BFF-side retry code) — rationale + rejection of option (a) documented in manifest.yaml + `H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler.cs` comments. **Material collateral finding**: while adding `FilePerEnvSettingsManifestTests.cs` (first-ever test against the REAL embedded manifest), discovered `FilePerEnvSettingsManifest.cs`'s YamlDotNet naming-convention never actually bound `iOptionsModule` — `ReadAsync()` has returned `Failure` for every per_env_settings entry (all 15, not just A39's 7) since task 201. Fixed via `[YamlMember(Alias = "iOptionsModule", ApplyNamingConventions = false)]`. This is a genuine bug fix squarely within "extend/fix existing component" (CLAUDE.md §11), but its blast radius exceeds A39's 7-entry scope — flagged prominently in `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` § 205c EXECUTION RESULTS for reviewer awareness before the next live provisioning run. **Deviation**: acceptance criterion 8's live-Azure "fresh Model 2 stamp + credential-level signal" integration test was NOT added — `IE2ETrapVerifier`/`H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs` (the natural home) were being concurrently modified by other in-flight tasks (205d / task-185-h13-aggregation) in this same shared worktree at execution time; touching them risked a real collision. Substituted L2-layer integration-style tests (`FilePerEnvSettingsManifestTests.cs` against the real manifest; `HttpHealthzProbeTests.cs` against real backoff-poll mechanics via a hand-rolled `HttpMessageHandler`, not `Mock<HttpMessageHandler>`) demonstrating the FIC-flap-tolerance mechanism; live-Azure credential-level verification remains task 186's obligation, consistent with A36/A37's own precedent. Build 0/0 (Tests + BFF API). `dotnet test` Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests: 1668 passed / 0 failed / 1 skipped (pre-existing). BFF publish size 45.07 MB compressed incl. PDBs vs 44.96 MB baseline — delta +0.11 MB (expected ≈0; A39 touches zero BFF-referenced code). code-review: 2 findings (1 blast-radius disclosure — addressed via punch-list annotation; 1 low-severity test-quality suggestion, not blocking). adr-check: 0 violations (ADR-028 A4 shape compliant; ADR-010/032/038 compliant). NOT committed — main session bundles 205c/d/e/f.</notes>

